From 65438d6cceb732222f35f00a1f288ba2d47ab085 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:32:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(ap): bills list, bill entry with coding, approval
 and journal screens [T-0086]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed: apps/web/src/purchases/ — /purchases/bills (every bill, state in words, who acts
next; "Enter a bill" only with ap.bill.enter), /purchases/bills/new (supplier, supplier invoice
number, dates, lines coded to expense/asset account and tax code from GET /ap/bill-coding; PUT
under an id chosen once per form) and /purchases/bills/$billId (coding with the API's GST and
totals, People involved, "Send for approval" / "Approve and post" with the SoD rule in words and
Approve disabled + aria-describedby when the API's outlook denies it, journal: engine preview on
request for a draft, the posted entry once approved). bill-logic.ts holds the words and form
checks (amounts stay strings). Shared files changed additively: env.tsx/App.tsx (purchases
client), router.tsx (3 routes), sections.ts (Purchases subpage link), main.tsx (purchases.css).
tests/e2e/web/bills.spec.ts: SS-UC05-08 at 1440 and 390 plus 4 behaviour tests.

Why: SS-UC05-08 (UC-05 bill entry and approval screens), UI principles P2-P7, P12-P13.

Validation: e2e spec RED first (6 failed, no screens; .agent/evidence/T-0086/red-e2e-bills.txt);
bill-logic.test.ts RED (module missing) then 5/5. Now bills.spec.ts 6/6 (axe WCAG 2.2 AA,
genericness probe, no horizontal scroll at 1440/390, <=1 primary, data-amount decimals);
all web e2e 71/71, 0 skipped; vitest unit+ui+web+api-unit 1102/1102; pnpm typecheck green;
eslint and prettier clean. Screenshots reviewed by eye: fixed truncated account/tax selects and
the coding totals rows (purchases.css). The fake fixture's company_id check was corrected for PUT
(company_id is in the body there and is asserted through the captured PUT body).

Next action: docs (card, register, decision log, follow-up card for the bills inbox screen).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
